    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Minor 7th",
      "body": "Count seven letters from C and you reach B, so C to B is a 7th. A **minor 7th** is 10 half steps, like C to B♭.\n\n**Why it matters:** The minor 7th is the \"7\" in chord names like G7, which you will meet in Unit 6. The original Star Trek theme opens with one.",
      "exampleMidi": [
        60,
        70
      ],
      "labels": {
        "60": "C",
        "70": "minor 7th"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Major 7th",
      "body": "A **major 7th** is 11 half steps, like C to B: just one half step short of the octave.\n\n**Why it matters:** It is the dreamy sound in \"maj7\" chords, which are all over soul, jazz and pop ballads.",
      "exampleMidi": [
        60,
        71
      ],
      "labels": {
        "60": "C",
        "71": "major 7th"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "show",
      "title": "Sevenths above C",
      "body": "B♭ is a minor 7th above C, and B is a major 7th.",
